<topic id="Toc29054">
      <title>Unsolicited HTTP Error Code Reporting</title>
      <body>
        <table colsep="1" frame="all" rowsep="1">
                    <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="0.6*"/>
            <colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="1.4*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Command</entry>
                <entry>Response</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>+HTTPERR</entry>
                <entry>+HTTPERR:&lt;id&gt;,&lt;errorcode&gt;</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>
        <p>Command Description:</p>
        <p>
This command is an unsolicited report message that displays the error status when an error occurs. </p>
        <p>Parameter Description: </p>
        <p>
&lt;id&gt;: Client instance created by the AT+HTTPCREATE command. </p>
        <p>
&lt;errorcode&gt;: Error code. Refer to Chapter 3. </p>
      </body>
    </topic>